meta {
  name: Create Connection
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/connections
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test FTP Connection",
    "type": "ftp"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.type: eq ftp
}

docs {
  `POST /api/v3/connections` -- creates an integration connection (FTP, SFTP,
  or Dropbox).

  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Created then deleted
  in the same test run (id was `6a9f1cc92b6fd055ffb7c7fe`) -- Connections has no
  downstream dependents in `TESTING_PLAN.md`, so this scratch resource was
  cleaned up per the ground rules rather than kept.

  `201 Created`. Response includes several null-defaulted FTP-specific fields
  not sent in the request (`url`, `port`, `user`, `source`, `last_processed`,
  `last_result_operation`) plus `use_tls: false`.

  ## Spec discrepancy -- type is a fixed lowercase enum (not a free string)
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s description for `ConnectionCreateInputDto.type` calls
  it a free string ("Dropbox, FTP, SFTP" given only as examples). **This is
  false** -- `type` is validated against a fixed, lowercase enum:
  `'dropbox'`, `'ftp'`, or `'sftp'`. Uppercase `"FTP"` also fails (case
  matters). See the 422 example below for the exact error message.

  ## Kept fixture (2026-09-21)
  A live "WC Test FTP Connection" was retained during the Sept-21 session:
  id `6aa98673a30ca5945169a25b`. GET by id confirms the null-defaulted fields
  shape (`last_processed`, `last_result_operation`, `source`, `url`, `port`,
  `user` all null; `use_tls: false`).
}

example {
  name: Create FTP Connection - Success (201)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Minimal body with name and lowercase type; null-defaulted connection-specific fields appear in the response.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/connections
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test FTP Connection",
        "type": "ftp"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa98673a30ca5945169a25b",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "name": "WC Test FTP Connection",
            "type": "ftp",
            "last_processed": null,
            "last_result_operation": null,
            "source": null,
            "url": null,
            "port": null,
            "user": null,
            "use_tls": false,
            "created": null,
            "modified": "2026-09-15T17:54:59.811000+00:00"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create Connection - Invalid Type (422, enum revealed)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. type is a fixed lowercase enum (dropbox, ftp, sftp) despite the spec describing it as a free string. Uppercase FTP also fails -- case matters.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/connections
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Nonsense Connection",
        "type": "ThisIsNotARealType123"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "type: Input should be 'dropbox', 'ftp' or 'sftp'"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
